[size=5][b][color=#E8C88A]Health Regen - Configurable[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Human and vampire health regeneration in one configurable mod. Choose separate rates for each form, keep regeneration outside combat, or allow it during combat. Both forms default to 1.5% per second.
<br />
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Stops healing at the limit[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Regeneration stops when your health bar or current vampire segment is full. This avoids the original vampire mod's repeated healing attempts at the limit.
<br />
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Choose your settings in [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Mod Setting Menu[/url], then press Apply to save and update gameplay.
<br />[list]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Human regeneration:[/color][/b] 0% to 5% per second; default 1.5%.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vampire regeneration:[/color][/b] 0% to 5% per second; default 1.5%.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Combat regeneration:[/color][/b] Off by default. Off means outside combat only; On also allows combat regeneration.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Restore vampire segments:[/color][/b] Off by default. On allows regeneration to restore lost segments toward full health.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Logging:[/color][/b] Choose Off, Error, Warning, Info or Debug. Warning is the default; Off is silent. Debug records detailed troubleshooting information in Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/UE4SS.log.[/*]
<br />[/list][color=#E6B980]Zero disables this mod's added regeneration for the selected form.[/color] Existing game regeneration bonuses remain separate. Regeneration does not revive a dead player.
<br />
<br />[size=3][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual configuration[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Launch the game once to create settings.ini, then close it. Open this file inside your The Blood of Dawnwalker game folder:
<br />[code]Dawnwalker&#92;Binaries&#92;Win64&#92;ue4ss&#92;Mods&#92;HealthRegeneration&#92;settings.ini[/code]The default settings are:
<br />[code][Settings]
<br />vampireRegenPercent = 1.5
<br />humanRegenPercent = 1.5
<br />combatRegen = 0
<br />restoreVampireSegments = 0
<br />logLevel = 2[/code]Change either regeneration rate using the steps above; 1.5 means 1.5% per second. For combatRegen and restoreVampireSegments, use 0 for Off or 1 for On. logLevel uses Off=0, Error=1, Warning=2, Info=3 and Debug=4. Save the file, restart the game and load a save to apply your changes.
<br />
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />[list]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vortex:[/color][/b] Install Health-Regen-Configurable.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual:[/color][/b] Copy the archive's Dawnwalker folder into your The Blood of Dawnwalker game folder, preserving the folder structure.[/*]
<br />[/list]
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Reporting Bugs and other issues[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />If you encounter an issue, set [b]Logging[/b] to [b]Debug[/b] in this mod’s Mod Setting Menu settings, apply the change, reproduce the issue. Then start either a bug report in the Bugs tab on Nexus (preferred method for me to track things), or at least start a new thread in comments and send me [b]Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/UE4SS.log[/b] from your game folder. Do not report unrelated bugs in other people's threads, please, this makes it impossible for me to track issues.
<br />
<br />
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Credits and source[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Idea credit goes to [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/387]Human Health Regen[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/391]Vampire Health Regen[/url] by KumasanGames. This implementation was completely rebuilt from stock game assets with its own configuration and runtime integration. Neither original mod's edited payloads are included.
<br />
<br />Thanks to Vercadi, UE4SS contributors and mmarcussa. Dependency notices are included. The game and its stock assets belong to Rebel Wolves and their respective rights holders.
